    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "but it doesn't feel like rebuilding. it feels like i'm just performing. like i'm a bad actor playing the role of a person who has a life, a career, and friends, but none of it is actually me anymore. the version of me that people cared about is gone. it's like the real me died when i lost my influence, and now i'm just a ghost haunting my own life. it's exhausting to keep up the charade.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Your exhaustion isn't weakness but the crushing weight of pretending when your authentic self has been too long ignored to survive.\nThe version of you that once mattered still exists but has been forced into hiding while a new, struggling self tries to breathe.\nInstead of hiding, let the people who knew you try to see you now as you are, because a real connection can only grow when the mask finally comes off.",
